# Kubernetes PODS - 
- single pod == single instance of an application running kube cluster
- pod can create and manage container in it.
- pod get an ip address & is shared by all cont inside the pod.
- pod is not a vm
- pod is a container - isolated solution.
- application code + dependies.

- pod is outer layer of the container
- why is pod if we have containers ?
= to handle the dynamic nature of the continers like ports, ip address - to manage in a better way.
= in pods container wont have the IP ADDRESS, its is given to pod.
- pods have multiple containers , but only in a speciic use cases we use the multiple containers in pods, if else its 1 pod = 1 container.
= 1 pod = 1 container.

